BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (standalone disk systems preceding MS-DOS. FAT12 became important through IBM PC DOS and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (MS-DOS floppy formats in the 1980s. Small sectors, restricted RAM and removable magnetic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (media favoured a single compact map of cluster ownership instead of indexed inodes or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (complex trees. Its longevity is explained by the simple disk layout and broad boot-ROM,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 592.0 Tm (BIOS, DOS and cross-platform compatibility, not by transaction integrity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (The FAT family evolved through FAT12, FAT16 and FAT32. These are not arbitrary names for) Tj ET
